      "question": "Does a bigger down payment make buying better?",
      "answer": "In this model, a bigger down payment helps buying. With 10% down, or $40,000, the cash to buy is $52,000. The payment rises to $2,472.95 because mortgage insurance is added. The break-even moves to year 30, compared with year 21 at 20% down."
    },
